# Root ignore rules (a template of the private repository, release/public/.gitignore:
# the subset of its python.gitignore-based file that this tree needs).
# Per-directory rules live beside what they cover: data/.gitignore (the
# exports and the private tree) and paper1/audit-training-kit/.gitignore
# (the fixture database and the scorer's outputs; a test pins it).

# Byte-compiled / packaging
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Environments
.venv
.env

# The working database, wherever a command creates it
*.db

# A file named *LOCAL-ONLY* declares itself uncommittable — the convention
# for a record that quotes real response text, which can live anywhere.
*LOCAL-ONLY*

# The preview debug build's scratch directory (written relative to the
# working directory, i.e. here when run from the repository root).
/preview_build_debug/

# No student data may enter this repository (README.md): a CSV a command
# writes anywhere — `export checks -o checks.csv` at the root — is ignored,
# so it cannot be added by mistake. The CSVs this tree ships are negated
# from the rule, location by location: the test fixtures, the alias and
# logging-regime tables of the drag-and-drop service, the Paper 1 board
# witness (by name — the sweep's path policy allows that one file under
# paper1/, so `-o paper1/checks.csv` stays ignored) and the audit-training
# kit (whose own .gitignore still keeps the scorer's outputs out). Keep real
# exports under data/private/ all the same.
*.csv
!src/tests/fixtures/*.csv
!src/proteus/services/dragndrop/aliases/*.csv
!src/proteus/services/dragndrop/logging_regimes/*.csv
!paper1/paper1-board-identity-witness-2026-10-07.csv
!paper1/audit-training-kit/**/*.csv
